<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarbagatai Mountains</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tarbagatai Mountains are a range on the border between eastern Kazakhstan and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altai-mountains">Altai</a> to the north-east and the Dzungarian Alatau to the south. They lay on steppe routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungaria">Dzungaria</a> and the Kazakh lands, and the town of Tacheng (Chuguchak) at their southern foot gave its name to the Qing district of Tarbagatai.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tarbagatai-mountains.jpg" alt="Tarbagatai Mountains" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tarbagatai2018 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GNPP_TARBAGATAI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
